{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T06:21:43.113Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"10","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (07dd7fa0). CONFIRMED, and WORSE than filed — a larger budget bought a strictly worse answer. On a repo whose snippet is 300 ESC bytes: budget 600 produced 'Index: cache-miss!N' with NO LOCATOR AT ALL, while budget 400 produced the locator plus source. Cause: at count == 1, available == budget; the render fits raw, termsafe.Bytes expands it past budget, and the only retry axis was count-- -\u003e 0 -\u003e nil, after which every prefix variant fails the len(formatted) \u003e 0 gate and the payload falls through to the telemetry tail. The locator could never expand (searchResultOnOneLine escapes path and name BEFORE measurement), so it was fitting the whole time. Fix adds an inner retry on the render WIDTH, scaled from what the attempt actually produced rather than what it was allowed — scaling from the allowance would let a block that came in under budget re-render unchanged forever. len(formatted) \u003e budget guarantees strictly smaller each pass so it terminates, and proportional scaling against the \u003c=6-byte-per-position escape bound stops it collapsing past widths that would have fitted; int64 guards 32-bit overflow. Fail-without-fix: 'budget 2000: dropped the result entirely' and 'budget 1200: lost the locator to escaped source'.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NFBNBB47WXT9GYS8Y178AT","targetId":"01M1NFBNBF8JYX7B6ZQX7Z3NZA","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NF973R4BZXAJK78QWWZ364"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
