{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:19:23.286Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"40","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"CONFIRMED and fixed in 3fc65542.\n\nReproduced the exact three-file case through the real grouping path (buildDefResponse -\u003e groupPartials), a throwaway test now deleted:\n  a.cs  public partial class Config  (owns field Config._timeout)\n  b.cs  public class Config          (memberless namesake)\n  c.cs  public partial class Config  (memberless part)\n\nObserved BEFORE the fix -- DeclarationTotal=3:\n  [0] class Config @ a.cs:3 sig=\"public partial class Config\" parts=[]\n  [1] class Config @ b.cs:3 sig=\"public class Config\"         parts=[]\n  [2] class Config @ c.cs:3 sig=\"public partial class Config\" parts=[]\nWith b.cs removed the same two partials merged (DeclarationTotal=1), so the namesake was the sole cause: matches are ordered by file path, b.cs sorts between a.cs and c.cs, it fails sharesMemberOwner, opens a new group and OVERWRITES byKey[key]; c.cs is then tested only against the namesake group ([b] declares no partial), fails, and stays split.\n\nObserved AFTER the fix -- DeclarationTotal=2:\n  [0] class Config @ a.cs:3 sig=\"public partial class Config\" parts=[PARTIAL(c.cs:3)]\n  [1] class Config @ b.cs:3 sig=\"public class Config\"         parts=[]\n\nFix is the remedy the finding prescribed: byKey now holds every group position seated under a key (map[string][]int) and a part is seated in the first compatible one. sharesMemberOwner is still the only predicate that merges, so this cannot over-merge -- it only stops an interposed namesake from hiding an earlier compatible group.\n\nRegression test: TestDefMergesPartialsSeparatedByANamesake (internal/cli/def_test.go).\nCompile-clean revert proof -- keeping the map[string][]int type but consulting only the newest position (byKey[key][max(0,len-1):]) builds clean (`go build ./...` -\u003e BUILD_OK) and the test fails:\n  --- FAIL: TestDefMergesPartialsSeparatedByANamesake (0.00s)\n      def_test.go:363: declarations = 3, want 2 (one merged partial type + one namesake)\n\nVerification: go build ./... clean, go vet ./internal/cli/ clean, gofmt clean, go test ./internal/cli/ ok (118.4s) after merging origin/main.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1P8YXN3S882SZJM1B51P0A3","targetId":"01M1P8YXNH61TTKXAX9NG4C290","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NF973R4BZXAJK78QWWZ364"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
